 hesitation in publicly expressing their opiaion that the changes in the law which are contemplated by this Bill would prove highly detrimental to the imterests of General Praotition- ers, that is to . to the interests of a great majority of those who are practising the healing art in this country. The Society, theref re, entreat their Licentiates to examine the pro- visions of this Bill for themselves, and to form their own opinion of its real scope and a aad they caution them, in tve meanwhile, against accepting Bull upon the opinion and recommendation of prominent feature of the Bill, which will not e.2ave attention, is this, that any who does not actually assume a med cal title (such as that of Physician, Surgeon, or Apothecary) will be at liberty to ise any branch of the profession without the nece-sity of undergoing an examination, or receivi anv medical education whatever. Consequently, Chemists and Druggists, should the Bill become law, will be legally entitled to practise any and every branch of the profession. By order of the Roolety of Apothecaries, seg? B. Urros, Clerk to the Society. Apothecaries'-hall, 26th Feb.. N=, READ ING-CASES for PROTECTING the ILLUsTRA TED LONDON NEWS during perusal. PORTFOLIOS to conta n Six Months’ ae © each. CASES for BIND ING the Volumes, 3s. 6d. each. May be obtaimed at the Office, 198, Strand; and of all Booksellers. Dire GALOP, by W. VANDERVELL, illustrated, price 2s. 6d. Also, the IMOGENE WALTZ, by same Composer, beautifully illustrated in colours, price 4s. Played nightly by Laurent's celebrated Baad. Sent postage-free. JULLIEN'S, Regent-stroet. IANOFORTES for HIRE at CHAPPELL’s. —The best of every description, by Broadwood, Collard, ond hrard, for Sa'e o- Hire.—50, New Bond-street. USICAL BOX DEPOT, 54, Cornhill, Lenten, for the sale of SWIS3 MUSICAL INSTRUMENTS, made by the celebrated Messrs. Nicole, Fréres, of Geneva. Large sizes, four airs, 14 in. long, £4; six airs, 18 in. lou, £6 6s.; eight airs, 20in. long, £8; a